# The eighth tooling step's measurement part: two trees' performance tests on
# one runner (`perf-ab`), `try`'s `perf --against` and `size`, and `size`'s
# `--profile`, `--at` and `--breakdown`.

# --- perf-ab ----------------------------------------------------------------

[break] a-failed-run-is-averaged-away
rule: A run of a side's performance tests that fails ends the comparison: a number from a failed test is not one to average.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: drive
find: let output = run(which, round)?;
replace: let output = run(which, round).unwrap_or_default();
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::a_run_that_fails_ends_it_and_a_measurement_on_one_side_is_said

[break] the-sides-keep-one-order-in-every-round
rule: The sides alternate which runs first, so that drift during the job falls on both alike.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: drive
find: for which in ab::order(round)
replace: for which in ab::order(0)
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::the_sides_run_in_turn_and_the_numbers_are_kept_for_each_round

[break] a-repeated-name-takes-its-last-value
rule: A name a run prints twice is the median of its values.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: numbers_in
find: .map(|(key, values)| (key, median(values)))
replace: .map(|(key, values)| (key, values[values.len() - 1]))
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::the_numbers_a_run_printed_are_read_and_a_repeated_name_is_its_median

[break] a-line-with-a-word-more-is-a-measurement
rule: A line is a measurement only with exactly a name, a value and a unit.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: numbers_in
find: (Some(name), Some(value), Some(unit), None)
replace: (Some(name), Some(value), Some(unit), _)
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::the_numbers_a_run_printed_are_read_and_a_repeated_name_is_its_median

[break] a-value-that-is-not-finite-is-a-measurement
rule: A value that is not finite (NaN, infinity) is left out, as a line that is not a number is.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: numbers_in
find: .filter(|value| value.is_finite())
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::the_numbers_a_run_printed_are_read_and_a_repeated_name_is_its_median

[break] the-median-of-an-even-count-is-the-upper-middle
rule: The median of an even number of values is the mean of the two in the middle.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: median
find: f64::midpoint(values[middle - 1], values[middle])
replace: values[middle]
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::the_median_of_an_even_count_is_between_the_middle_two

[break] ranges-that-touch-are-apart
rule: Two sides' ranges are apart only when they do not overlap: equal points overlap.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: verdict
find: let apart = head_least > base_most || head_most < base_least;
replace: let apart = head_least >= base_most || head_most <= base_least;
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::a_difference_is_apart_only_where_the_ranges_do_not_overlap

[break] a-faster-head-is-not-apart
rule: A head whose whole range is below the base's is apart, as one above it is.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: verdict
find: let apart = head_least > base_most || head_most < base_least;
replace: let apart = head_least > base_most;
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::a_difference_is_apart_only_where_the_ranges_do_not_overlap

[break] the-percentage-is-of-the-head
rule: The change's percentage is of the base's figure.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: verdict
find: change / base * 100.0
replace: change / head * 100.0
caught-by:
    perf_ab::tests::a_difference_is_apart_only_where_the_ranges_do_not_overlap

[break] the-tests-run-four-at-a-time
rule: The performance tests run one at a time, so that two measurements never share the machine.
file: xtask/src/perf_ab.rs
in: nextest_arguments
